<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="859bfb4f">The benefits manager has visibility into the portfolio of programs and projects and works closely with the sponsors,
program managers, and project managers throughout the course of the engagement. The benefits manager specializes in
selecting the appropriate benefits management method for a given client context. Using this knowledge and general
facilitation skills, the benefits manager conducts workshops to identify potential benefits and guides the benefits
quantification process. The benefits manager plays a key role in building the business case and the benefits realization
plan as well as in designing the required tracking mechanisms to report progress to the stakeholders. The benefits manager
works to see that the benefits realization plan is executed correctly and that the benefits are reviewed regularly
according to the established review schedule. Finally, the benefits manager works with the program manager during the
program closure phase to verify that proper ownership for any remaining actions, which may be needed so that the
realization of the benefits are transitioned to business as usual (BAU).</attribute>
</Element>
